1. Create an S3 Bucket for Website Hosting

Go to AWS Console → S3 → Create Bucket

Enter a unique bucket name

Choose region

Disable “Block all public access” temporarily (for initial testing)

Leave defaults and create the bucket

2. Upload Website Files to S3

Open your bucket → Click Upload

Add all your static files (HTML/CSS/JS)

Upload them

3. Configure S3 Bucket Permissions

Add this bucket policy to allow public read access (testing only):

{
   "Version": "2012-10-17",
   "Statement": [
       {
           "Sid": "AddPerm",
           "Effect": "Allow",
           "Principal": "*",
           "Action": "s3:GetObject",
           "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::YOUR_BUCKET_NAME/*"
       }
   ]
}


Replace YOUR_BUCKET_NAME with your actual bucket name.

4. Enable Static Website Hosting in S3

Open Properties tab → Static website hosting

Enable

Set index.html as the Index document

Save

Copy the Bucket Website Endpoint and test it in your browser

⚠️ It loads but shows "Not Secure" because S3 doesn't provide HTTPS.

Re-enable Block all public access after testing.

5. Create a CloudFront Distribution

Go to CloudFront → Create Distribution

Origin Domain: select your S3 bucket

Default Root Object: index.html

CloudFront automatically provides HTTPS

Create the distribution

When complete:

Copy the Distribution Domain Name

Access your website securely using this domain
